---
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
---

<Docs title="Getting started" description="Install mitame, pick an era and add your first components in a React project.">
  <h1>Getting started</h1>
  <p class="lede">mitame copies component source into your React project. Three steps, then it's your code.</p>

  <h2>1. Initialize</h2>
  <p>Run this in your project root. It writes <code class="inline-code">mitame.json</code> and copies the helpers and the theme CSS.</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`npx mitame init                  # Aqua, the default
npx mitame init --theme liquid    # or liquid glass
npx mitame init --theme platinum  # or Mac OS 8/9 gray`} />

  <h2>2. Import the styles once</h2>
  <p>In your global CSS (paths follow the <code class="inline-code">dir</code> in <code class="inline-code">mitame.json</code>, <code class="inline-code">src/components/mitame</code> by default):</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="css" code={`@import "./components/mitame/themes/base.css";
@import "./components/mitame/themes/y2k/aqua.css";

/* Using Tailwind v4? Add the bridge after tailwindcss for bg-mi-accent, rounded-mi-lg, ... */
@import "tailwindcss";
@import "./components/mitame/themes/tailwind.css";`} />

  <h2>3. Pick the era</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="html" code={`<html data-theme="aqua">                   <!-- follows the device light/dark -->
<html data-theme="aqua" data-mode="light">  <!-- always light, strict 2001 -->
<html data-theme="liquid" data-mode="dark"> <!-- always dark -->`} />
  <p>Themes also work on any element, so one page can show several eras.</p>

  <h2>4. Add components</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`npx mitame add button dialog select
npx mitame list   # everything you can add`} />
  <CodeBlock code={`import { Button } from "@/components/mitame/ui/button";

export function Save() {
  return <Button variant="primary">Save</Button>;
}`} />
  <p>
    <code class="inline-code">add</code> follows imports, so <code class="inline-code">select</code> brings the hooks and icons it needs. Files you already have are kept; <code class="inline-code">--overwrite</code> replaces only what you name.
  </p>

  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>React 19. No other runtime dependencies.</li>
    <li>Browsers: Chrome and Edge 114+, Safari 17+, Firefox 125+ (Popover API).</li>
    <li>Tailwind is optional.</li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
